{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"Discovered from sole-curbable-stinkpot (9a71-ba9b-89d0-4cb8). The original framing (\"ACLI\n'command cancelled' is emitted and swallowed\") understated this: the string is not swallowed\nnoise, it is a FAILURE COUNTED AS A SUCCESS. Retitled and re-scoped to the real defect.\n\n## Context / Problem\n\nIn the outbound link-apply loop, a cancelled ACLI link delete is counted as an applied link.\n`RECON: batch_outcome ... error=None links_applied=N` therefore reports work that never\nhappened, and the silent-noop canary is blind to it by construction.\n\nEvidence, run 31535962079 raw log:\n\n- `ACLI stderr: X Error: command cancelled` occurrences = 15\n- sum of every `links_applied=` across the whole pass    = 15\n- occurrences of `update_one: ... failed`                = 0\n\nExact 1:1, per-ticket not just in aggregate: 2 cancellations -> REB-1305 `links_applied=2`;\n1 -> REB-1308 `=1`; 2 -> REB-1398 `=2`; 2 -> REB-1442 `=2`; 1 -> REB-1538/1656/1666 `=1`;\n2 -> REB-1694 `=2`; 1 -> REB-184/2114/2321 `=1`. Every ticket with zero cancellations reports\n`links_applied=0`. Zero links were actually removed in that pass.\n\nMechanism, `dispatch_one.py` `_update_one_dispatch_links`:\n\n    try:\n        _call_with_retry(client.delete_issue_link, link_id)\n        _links_applied += 1\n    except subprocess.CalledProcessError:\n        # ...treated as idempotent 404/409...\n        _links_applied += 1\n\nThat arm has NO print — which is why zero `update_one: ... failed` lines appear and why this\nlooked like free-floating noise. Its stated rationale (\"self-healing — the differ recomputes\nthe REMOVE next pass\") does not hold, because the cause is DETERMINISTIC: `link create` and\n`link delete` prompt for confirmation and are run with `stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL`, so the\nprompt reads EOF and ACLI reports `command cancelled` on every pass, forever.\n\nThis is the bug 44de silent-divergence class. `REBAR_RECONCILER_FAIL_SILENT_NOOP` cannot catch\nit: the canary tests `computed > 0 and applied == 0`, and this arm inflates `applied` to equal\n`computed`.\n\nRoot cause is CONFIRMED, not suspected (see ticket comment): `acli 1.3.19-stable` — the exact\nversion the fleet caches — documents `--yes` on BOTH subcommands (`Confirm link creation\nwithout prompting` / `Confirm link deletion without prompting`), and neither call site passes\nit. Verified against the link subcommands themselves, not inferred from the `workitem delete`\nsibling. Note `--json` is genuinely rejected there (story 25ae, correct); `--yes` is genuinely\naccepted. Conflating the two flags produced the original \"verify before adding\" caution.\n\n## Approach\n\nTwo edits: stop the lie, then remove its cause.\n\n**1. Stop counting failures as applied** (`dispatch_one.py`). Add a `_links_failed` counter.\nThe delete handler's `except subprocess.CalledProcessError` arm keeps its idempotent rationale\nbut narrows to genuine idempotent signatures — stderr matching `404`, `409`, `does not exist`,\nor `not found` (case-insensitive; absent stderr is NOT idempotent). Those still count toward\n`_links_applied`, so a benign concurrent removal does not become a new hard failure. Every\nother `CalledProcessError` increments `_links_failed` and prints, as does the trailing\n`except Exception` arm and the `set_relationship` (create) handler. Every arm stays non-fatal:\nthe loop does not unwind. `links_failed` rides the existing `subop` dict through\n`apply_handlers.py` onto the outcome and is printed in the `batch_outcome` line — an additive\nfield; existing fields keep their meaning. This alone makes the canary able to fire.\n\n**2. Remove the cause** (`acli_graph.py`). Pass `--yes` to `workitem link create` and\n`workitem link delete`, with a comment citing the 1.3.19-stable help verification, mirroring\nthe existing `workitem delete` precedent at `acli.py:714-724` (bug 3256 / live cfd6 probe).\n\n**Deliberately NOT doing:** no `AcliCancelledError` / cancellation fast-abort. With `--yes`\nremoving the prompt, a dedicated exception type is speculative machinery for a path that\nshould stop occurring; edit 1 makes any residual failure visible, which is the durable\nprotection.\n\n**Disjointness.** This is the OUTBOUND ACLI path. It does not touch change 1640's\n`_AUTH_FAILURE_MARKERS` / `AcliAuthError` (credential rejection, a different marker set and a\ndifferent call path), and it does not touch the inbound-links state work. No shared edit\nregion with either.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/dispatch_one.py` — `_links_failed`; narrowed idempotent\n  arm; create-side failure counting.\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/apply_handlers.py` — carry `links_failed` onto outcome.\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/applier.py` — print `links_failed` in `batch_outcome`.\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira/acli_graph.py` — `--yes` on both link cmds.\n- `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/mutate/test_outbound_link_failure_accounting.py` (new).\n- `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/mutate/test_outbound_update_combined.py` — existing subop\n  assertions updated for the new key.\n- `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/apply/test_silent_noop_canary.py` — existing canary assertions\n  updated for the narrowed applied-count.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Happy path: a create + delete that both succeed report `links_applied=2 links_failed=0`.\n- Regression (the defect): `delete_issue_link` raising `CalledProcessError` with\n  `command cancelled` stderr yields `links_applied=0 links_failed=1`, NOT today's\n  `links_applied=1`.\n- Idempotent path preserved: the same failure with `404` stderr still counts applied,\n  `links_failed=0`.\n- Absent stderr is not treated as idempotent: `CalledProcessError` with `stderr=None` counts\n  failed.\n- Edge: `set_relationship` failure increments `links_failed`, call returns normally (non-fatal).\n- Argv: `link create` and `link delete` argv both contain `--yes`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A cancelled `delete_issue_link` (non-idempotent stderr) no longer increments\n      `links_applied` — verified by a test asserting `links_applied=0, links_failed=1`.\n- [ ] A failed `delete_issue_link` with idempotent stderr (404/409/does-not-exist/not-found)\n      still counts applied — verified by a test asserting `links_applied=1, links_failed=0`.\n- [ ] `CalledProcessError` with `stderr=None` counts failed, not applied — verified by test.\n- [ ] A failed `set_relationship` increments `links_failed` and does not unwind the pass —\n      verified by a test asserting `links_applied=0, links_failed=1` and normal return.\n- [ ] The `RECON: batch_outcome` line for an `update` includes `links_failed=<n>` — verified\n      by a test capturing stderr and asserting the substring.\n- [ ] `workitem link create` and `workitem link delete` argv both include `--yes` — verified\n      by a test asserting the flag is present in each command list.\n- [ ] `make lint`, `make typecheck`, and the reconciler unit suite pass."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786525905781168001,"uuid":"cf693993-0804-40d2-b71f-eb25eee08407"}